+"""Everyday Home: an invented household home folder, for walking Graphite as a person uses a computer (Graphite 1.0 X3).
+
+The owner, 26 November 2026: "Should we simulate general user operations instead of the same rail tests?" Rail Demo is the
+engineering desk; Everyday Home is the ordinary computer around it: letters, a lease, a manual, photos, a messy Downloads
+folder, a household budget in Calc, a little music, a USB stick with holiday photos. Every name, address, amount, picture
+and sentence in it was made up for the purpose, and the papers say so (NOTICE on every page and in every file that has
+words). Nothing here is anyone's real data.
+
+What it holds ("today" is TODAY, Thursday 26 November 2026):
+
+    Documents   "Letter to the landlord.odt" (a Writer letter), "Lease - Flat 3 Orchard Row.pdf" (three pages),
+                "Washing machine manual.pdf" (four pages), "Household budget 2026.ods" (a Calc budget: a "Spending" sheet of
+                dated rows with a category and an exact amount, October and November, and a "Plan" sheet)
+    Pictures    a dozen small photos, drawn here with Qt (no camera, no EXIF): their captions are their file names
+    Downloads   a messy mix: bills and statements as PDFs (one bill twice), photos (one twice), a screenshot, an .ods
+                template, a .zip of three photos, a recipe as text
+    Music       two short sounds (WAV, made here from whole numbers)
+    Desktop     a shopping list and a to-do list
+    the USB stick   a folder of its own (DCIM/100DEMO with four photos) that a stand-in drive shows when it is mounted
+
+The groceries of November in the budget come to GROCERIES_NOVEMBER (244.65) exactly; October's to 204.60. Amounts are
+written as decimal text and summed here as Fractions, never as floating point.
+
+The door: `python -m workbench.everyday_demo FOLDER` builds it in FOLDER (a new or empty throwaway folder): the home folder
+in FOLDER/home, the stick's contents in FOLDER/usb, Graphite's workspace where a fresh install keeps it (FOLDER/home/Concern
+/Ledger) and a profile of its own in FOLDER/profile. It never writes into the home folder of the person at the computer:
+the window that walks it is started with environment(FOLDER), whose HOME is FOLDER/home. Deterministic: the same bytes
+every time (digests()). No network, no model, no LibreOffice needed (the OpenDocument files are written directly).
+
+    from workbench import everyday_demo
+    made = everyday_demo.build(folder)             # the home, the stick, the workspace's folder -> what was made
